ryan reynolds is an actor with a resume  full of hits and misses  he's not afraid to take on the silliest  of roles and sometimes he even pokes fun  at his biggest mistakes  he might be a superstar but simply  attaching his name to a project doesn't  guarantee it's going to be a success you  shut your  damn trash mouth not every film reynolds  releases is going to be deadpool  no matter how big the budget or how  great the supporting cast is  sometimes an actor will have a failure  on their hands that's the case with one  of reynold's biggest movies of the last  few years  it was one we were confident would get a  sequel at first however  we just learned there are no franchise  plans for this popular netflix original  in 2019 netflix released six underground  a high octane action flick with ryan  reynolds as the lead and michael bay  directing on a 150 million dollar budget  the film was full of pulse-pounding  action sequences and dramatic explosions  in a promotional video reynolds called  it the most michael bay movie that  michael bay has ever michael bade  the action comedy flick centers around a  billionaire known as  one played by reynolds he fakes his  death to create a vigilante crew that  takes down terrorists  and other scummy criminals the team  includes five other members who are  named  two three four five and six creative  right  the film sounded good on paper but when  it finally landed on netflix in december  of 2019  it was ripped to shreds by reviewers it  currently holds a 38  critic score on rotten tomatoes so it's  not suicide squad level bad  but still pretty terrible the problem it  was overstuffed silly and a little  too michael bay robert levin of newsday  described the film perfectly  saying this is a terrible action movie  that utilizes michael bay's worst  instincts and  none of his best despite being one of  netflix's most viewed original movies of  all time  six underground was a miss in every  other way it was so bad that netflix's  film chief scott stuber told variety a  sequel  definitely isn't coming the netflix boss  admitted  we didn't feel like we got there on that  one creatively it was a nice hit but at  the end of the day we didn't feel like  we nailed the mark to justify coming  back again  there just wasn't that deep love for  those characters or that world  netflix never confirmed a sequel for the  movie but it was largely suspected based  on its high viewership  going off of stuber's recent comments  however it looks like numbers aren't the  only important thing  not only does a netflix original need to  attract a large audience but it also  needs to resonate with those viewers  six underground just didn't have people  talking at the water cooler and the ones  who were weren't talking about it in a  good way  netflix is choosing to move forward with  sequels for debut films that had a  positive response  both quantitatively and qualitatively in  the action genre that catalog  includes the old guard and extraction  just to name a few  so ryan reynolds and company won't be  reuniting for six underground two  seven underground or two underground too  furious  but with plenty of other films on his  docket he's probably not too worried  about it at this point  scott stuber further expressed what is  of utmost importance to the folks at  netflix when it comes to making original  content  we have to be more consistent at making  these movies more culturally relevant  and putting them in the zeitgeist  we know the audience is there for these  movies but i want people to feel that  impact in their conversations with  friends and colleagues  where they're saying did you hear about  this movie old guard we've done it but  we haven't done it consistently  it all comes back to those water cooler  moments which yes is twitter these days  and unfortunately for six underground it  trended for all the wrong reasons  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

